solution:
**Given:**

Selling Price (SP) = ₹2,600

Profit Percentage = 30%

**Formula used:**

Cost Price (CP) = dfrac{SP}{1 + dfrac{Profit \%}{100}}

**Calculation:**

CP = dfrac{2600}{1 + dfrac{30}{100}}

⇒ CP = dfrac{2600}{1 + 0.30}

⇒ CP = dfrac{2600}{1.30}

⇒ CP = ₹2,000

**∴ The correct answer is option 2.**
